{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1486654-trinity-reincarnation-some-basic-ideas-for-a-post-post-apocalyptic-fantasysetting","id":1486654,"title":"[Trinity Reincarnation] Some basic ideas for a post-post-apocalyptic Fantasysetting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-16T12:34:10-07:00","id":1486654,"title":"[Trinity Reincarnation] Some basic ideas for a post-post-apocalyptic Fantasysetting","content":"Just thinking out loud: The Trinity Continuum is set in a multiverse. So why shouldn't there be a parallel world or alternative timeline somewhere that corresponds to common fantasy tropes, or at least some of them? For example, how about the following very rough idea:<br /> <br /> In Timeline X, the history of the Trinity Universe proceeds pretty much as we know it - but unfortunately only up to the Aberrant War. In this timeline, the Chinese government's idea of driving the Novas from Earth by threatening nuclear suicide goes devatastingly wrong. Some unfortunate Chinese officer loses his nerve and actually presses the red button! What follows, is what was to be expected. Thermonuclear warheads strike randomly all over the world. A decades long nuclear winter follows. Billions die. When the dust settles and the first rays of the sun manage reach the surface of the planet once again, not much is left of humanity. Those few people, who are still there, have to start again from scratch.<br /> <br /> 2000 years later:<br /> The earth is green and flourishing again - and humanity is also somewhat florishing again. But it has not yet reached the technological level of the old world. The numerous small kingdoms all over the world have a rather medieval level of technology.<br /> <br /> There are once again galleys crossing the mediterranean sea - this time in service of a new &quot;roman&quot; empire based on Corsica. This new empire recently allied with the ancient, subterran civilisation below the land, that once was the german Ruhrgebiet.<br /> On the other side of the planet, dozens of temple-cities, each ruled by its own &quot;god&quot;, fight for dominance over the countless islands of what once was south east asia. They have recently re-invented the cannon and are expanding rapidly - in territories as well as in riches - despite the fact, that they are constantly fighting each other. Just the accursed deserts of what was once China are feared by their priests (but not by their adventurers).<br /> Across the pacific ocean, on the northamerican continent, the mighty mississipian Riverkings dwell in castles, that resemble european castles of old. They uphold the one true faith in the one true goddess and uphold the ideals of chivalry. At least, thats what they tell their peasants.<br /> <br /> The Aberrant War was mythologically reinterpreted as a war of the gods. Legacies of the old world are misunderstood as magic - and you can't blame the inhabitants of the &quot;new&quot; Earth either. Thousands of dead Novas have altered the space-time structure of the Earth in such a way that apparently &quot;paranormal&quot; phenomena frequently haunt people. Mutations have ensured that other hominid species now exist alongside the original Homo sapiens. Humans live in peace with some of them. With others they do not.<br /> <br /> Psiads and talents are more common in this new age than they were in the 20th and 21st centuries, so that supposed mages, legendary swordsmen and similar fellows who otherwise only exist in fantasy novels are now actually running around. The few remaining (or newly created) Novas, on the other hand, are considered gods and mostly live isolated from humans.<br /> <br /> Aeon also still exists, but in this age it is a mysterious secret society that tries to fight evil from the shadows, defend humanity and help it back to a higher level of development. The problem with this is that in many distorted myths about the Aberrant War, Aeon is considered complicit in the end of the world!<br /> <br /> The ideas about the whole thing were stolen from &quot;Empire of the East&quot;, from too many J-RPGs to count and, of course, from Exalted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T17:50:18-07:00","id":1486700,"title":"","content":"This sounds really cool. I can see the resemblance to Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:32:53-07:00","id":1486740,"title":"","content":"As with 'we can recreate fantasy tropes' - you can have also Novas, Psions or Talents easily in previous eras. Imagine mass Novas awakening in medieval times ( various 'saints' + <b>Assassin's Creed game</b> series? ) or in Ancient Greece. Like Novas as our ancestors gods and demigods... \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> You do not need to imagine it, as it's exactly how <b>Trinity Aegis</b> will play out! I shorten description for it as '<b>Assassin's Creed: Odyssey</b> - but with TC Novas! ( And maybe other templates )' \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-waw1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/287955410_10218049694748801_4750717136127288290_n.jpg?_nc_cat=111&amp;ccb=1-7&amp;_nc_sid=5cd70e&amp;_nc_ohc=lGPq2Satp1cAX-mS5t0&amp;tn=HtFYOETvXEa1iIZY&amp;_nc_ht=scontent-waw1-1.xx&amp;oh=00_AT-zJ1DBxAR06zccvPxFukV5R-KzJtJkjhSHkf1Sx-zO2Q&amp;oe=62D9B1E8\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:49:48-07:00","id":1486742,"title":"","content":"I am looking forward to that so much (as I do for pretty much every new part of trinity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Aegis, by the way, is also the reason why I'm putting this idea here in an alternative future of the Trinity Continuum rather than in a past age.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking further into the blue for the post-post-apocalyptic stuff:<br /> <br /> Blight Zones are of course a factor even 2000 years after the Aberrant War. In fact, even more so than in the Trinity Aeon timeline, since the war escalated much more violently.<br /> For one thing, in the phase immediately after the war, the mutation rate of animals and plants was increased throughout the planet. As a result, in the timeline of &quot;Trinity Reincarnation&quot; (we really need a better name) there are several alien species of animals and plants that do not yet exist in our present.<br /> On the other hand, pretty much every human kingdom on the planet knows of some cursed forests, demonic deserts and &quot;lands of evil&quot; from which monsters crawl with regularity to threaten kingdoms.<br /> Probably the biggest blight zone of all is China. It was over this land that the full wrath of the Aberrants was unleashed after the nuclear missiles were launched - with the result that, 2000 years later, the entire land still resembles Mordor or the Chaos Deserts from Warhammer Fantasy, rather than an area one would expect to find on Earth.<br /> And to give a brief overview of the ideas about this age so far:<br /> <br /> The technology level of most of the &quot;civilised&quot; kingdoms is broadly equivalent to the High Middle Ages, but the use of PSI powers and all sorts of &quot;magical artefacts&quot; ensures that the world actually looks more like what you would see in fantasy role-playing games and less like something you would think of as a &quot;realistic Middle Ages&quot;.<br /> <br /> Overall, there is no kingdom or empire that really has global dominance. Instead, as in pre-modern days, there are several major local powers and &quot;clusters&quot; of mostly quarrelling petty kingdoms.<br /> <br /> The Corsican Empire dominates large parts of North Africa and Europe and was an aggressive imperialist power 500 years ago. Over the centuries, however, the empire became more saturated and &quot;friendly&quot;. Today, the &quot;Pax Corsicana&quot; ensures that the European and North African city-states are a comparatively peaceful, prosperous and cosmopolitan part of the world. The price, however, is decadence and technological stagnation. In the last four centuries, there has not been a single new technological invention in the Corsican Empire.<br /> Recently, the Corsican empire has allied itself with its former enemies, the &quot; subterraneans &quot; - the descendants of German, Austrian and Swiss bunker dwellers who now, 2000 years later, resemble nothing so much as dwarves from classic fantasy literature.<br /> The alliance is shaky and many a hardliner would rather see war again.<br /> <br /> On the North American continent, the &quot;river kings&quot; have established a group of empires that bear a striking resemblance to the kingdoms of medieval Europe. They are united by a common religion to a benevolent &quot;goddess&quot; who resides in the Great Lakes (a 2000-year-old Nova). They are separated by all kinds of succession squabbles and honour trades. All the river kingdoms are on the east bank of the Mississippi, because east of the Mississippi the &quot;Goddess&quot; has healed over the centuries the damage once caused by Wycoff's Blight. West of the Mississippi, however, is still a massive blight zone. The river kings are permanently crusading against the monster hordes that keep springing up there.<br /> <br /> In Indonesia, seven powerful empires have established themselves, each founded by huge city-states. Each of these seven empires is ruled by an immortal, divine ruler. It is unclear whether these immortal rulers are novas or pure fictions. Military expansion and progress have ensured that each of these realms has military and technological resources equivalent to those of Europe in the early 17th century. Unfortunately, this also tempts the powerful of the Seven Kingdoms into similar follies. Most of Southeast Asia and northern Australia are either tributary or direct colonies of one of the seven Indonesian empires. Attempts to expand into India, however, have all failed so far.<br /> <br /> South America is a conglomerate of several small kingdoms and empires. At one time, all these small kingdoms were tributary to the mighty Brazilian Empire. However, this is in the process of collapsing, as the last emperor has left behind ten heirs who see themselves as equals and who are now carving up Brazil in a massive war of succession. As a result, all the old treaties and alliances that had made South America a comparatively peaceful place over the past 150 years are no longer valid. Intrigues are spun and armies of knights are deployed.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T04:03:10-07:00","id":1486753,"title":"","content":"You got to High Middle Ages feel - but why not Neo Stone Age from Horizon series? You can have all 'monsters and magic' trappings - but with trial culture. On the other hand - even mass <b>Aberrant War</b> would not destroy civilisation to the level of Stone Age level - you literally need to destroy every large settlement ( beyond 500 people ) and 'turn off' all electrics controling Novas, Psions and the rest... Maybe your Neo Middle Ages is much more fesiable... \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn2.unrealengine.com/hzn-zdce-storefront-2560x1440-v2-2560x1440-378073920.jpg?h=720&amp;resize=1&amp;w=1280\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T13:12:18-07:00","id":1486791,"title":"","content":"Hmmm....taking Horizon Zero Dawn as an (additional) inspiration is a quite good idea. Having neo-medival AND neo-neolithic areas in one world is no contradiction at all. &quot;Tech-levels&quot; are seldom dispersed evenly, especially if the world is much less globalised than our modern one. There should be ample room to spare for tribal cultures. (This is, after all, also the same route, Horizon Zero Dawn takes. Not all tribes have the same stone-age-vibe.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T02:55:40-07:00","id":1486975,"title":"","content":"Here's a better visualization of the whole thing - and focused on North America in 4060 A.D for the time being. Since I don't yet have a bright idea for proper names, the designations are all provisional, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Blightzone:</b> this area still goes back to what was once called &quot;Wycoffs Blight&quot;. The Blightzone has receded and shifted somewhat over the course of 20 centuries, but it is still a polluted wasteland full of monsters and mutations<br /> <br /> <b>Crusades!:</b> This area is technically part of the Blight Zone, but it is the main war zone between the mutant tribes from the Blight Zone and the River Kingdoms. The River Kingdoms keep trying to build border fortresses and establish villages here. So far, this has always led to disasters.<br /> <br /> <b>River Kingdoms:</b> As mentioned above - A hodgepodge of medium and small kingdoms whose technological development is roughly equivalent to the High Middle Ages. All River Kingdoms share the same religion, but that doesn't stop them from warring with each other quite often. All kingdoms but one are feudal states. Former Michigan, however, is a theocracy and the spiritual center of the River Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> <b>Mountain-Tribes: </b>a cluster of tribes and clans that fluctuate technologically somewhere between the Neolithic and the early Iron Age. Resemble in many ways classic fantasy barbarians from Sword&amp;Sorcery stories.<br /> <br /> <b>Eastern City States:</b> A group of city republics engaged in transatlantic trade.<br /> <br /> <b>Satrapies of Snake Workshipers:</b> In the south of the former USA some communities of &quot;Snake Handlers&quot; survived the apocalypse. Their descendants now live there in small towns and build temple towers out of mud bricks. The religion they belong to can still be seen to have evolved from Christianity. Since the snake worshippers have built their culture on fragmentary Old Testament traditions, the area is vaguely reminiscent of the Near East of antiquity. For religious reasons, there are regular conflicts with the River Kingdoms, but these are usually quickly settled when major threats arise in the Blight Zone.<br /> <br /> <b>Faux-Asian Empire:</b> In the former California, an empire has established itself whose cultural roots lie in Asia. California itself is comparatively urbanized. The former San Francisco is now home to the imperial court. In addition, this empire claims some territory outside of California, but it is sparsely populated.<br /> <br /> <b>Holdings of the Brazilian Empire: </b>Mexico also had some medieval kingdoms, but they were subjugated by Brazil. Brazilian rule over Mexico was always shaky, however, and is now more or less non-existent, thanks to the War of Succession far to the south.<br /> <br /> <b>Western and Southern Neo-neolithic Tribes:</b> A large collection of diverse tribes and clans whose level of technology is roughly comparable to that of the Native Americans just before the arrival of the Europeans. So definitely highly developed, but with little metalworking. (These areas would be the &quot;Horizon-Zero-Dawn Corner&quot;, so to speak).<br /> <br /> One thing, of course, is important: the whole thing was made up by a guy from Germany, who I'm sure is missing a whole bunch of details when it comes to North America. If any Americans looking in here have some better ideas, they are of course welcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/r5vcB8B/North-America-in-4060-AD.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}